#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:5
#: da4512b8c2e84c1a81183c0ab71fdf4a
msgid "Traditional Helicopter – Swashplate Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:7
#: 504f643d2d5e4151a4d8549a892b393c
msgid ""
"The swashplate is designed to take the servo inputs that are based on the"
" pilot’s pitch, roll, and collective commands and translate them to "
"individual blade pitch inputs. There are many different servo "
"arrangements for both three and four servo swashplates. The swashplate "
"library covers all of the popular configurations for both three and four "
"servo swashplates. If you have a unique swashplate, you can also use the "
"generic three servo swashplate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:14
#: 278f6c11216e4d16aa7268c0abbd5d66
msgid ""
"Linearize Servo is a feature that you can use for both three and four "
"servo swashplates. However, it is optional for the three servo "
"swashplates as there is no chance for binding. It will most likely always"
" be required for four servo swashplates because of the potential for "
"binding in a four point attachment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:19
#: cd507aa6b7be45c0bc00e63269945517
msgid ""
"The following video covers the swashplate setup and leveling the "
"swashplate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:23
#: 13904207fa0f40f3b1e535e5bf2a6ad5
msgid ""
"This video covers setting up the min collective, max collective, zero "
"thrust collective, max cyclic and stabilize collective curve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:28
#: ec2063d72c304038bdab4be65c5bd17a
msgid "Before You Begin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:30
#: 4c2aa79863954677ab806a136b51b231
msgid ""
"Prior to beginning the swashplate set up, be sure that your helicopter "
"control linkages are set up in accordance with the assembly instructions."
" In order to make accurate blade pitch measurements, make the rotor shaft"
" perpendicular to the ground by using shims underneath the landing gear "
"as shown in the picture below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:38
#: 1b4eb44d0f0e46a8bee03ef7cca01acd
msgid ""
"Lastly, it is possible if you haven’t adjusted your tail rotor linkage, "
"or your throttle linkage in the case of a gas engine, you could have "
"binding occur while doing the swashplate set up. This is due to the "
":ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>` feature providing manual servo settings that "
"drive the servos to the min and max values. This includes the tail rotor "
"servo and the throttle servo due to throttle curve settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:45
#: d64cdaf8c5214d76ba8c0d9a3678c568
msgid "Select Swashplate Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:47
#: 8314a5fb8f294f328b532942bdaa358f
msgid ""
"Below are the swashplate type selections using the "
":ref:`H_SW_TYPE<H_SW_TYPE__AP_MotorsHeli_Single>` parameter.  The "
"diagrams shown label the servo attach positions as Servo 1, Servo 2 and "
"Servo 3 for the three servo swashplate types.  These also correspond to "
"the default output functions for servo outputs 1 thru 3 on the autopilot "
"for the servos used with these swashplate types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:50
#: bc91ff7ff6f343e68742aa4eb964fa23
msgid ""
"For single heli, the servo function assigned to Servo 1 is motor 33, "
"Servo 2 is motor 34, and Servo 3 is motor 35.  These assignments are the "
"same for swashplate 1 for a dual heli frame.  Swashplate 2 for a dual "
"heli defaults to servo outputs 4, 5, and 6 with motors 36, 37 and 38 "
"assigned respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:55
#: 0937c74e89fa4a119d02fb2eae331321
msgid ""
"For four servo swashplates, the fourth servo (Servo 5) on the single heli"
" frame defaults to servo output 5 and is assigned motor 37. For the dual "
"heli frame, the fourth servo (Servo 7) on swashplate 1 defaults to servo "
"output 7 and is assigned motor 39. The fourth servo (Servo 8) on "
"swashplate 2 defaults to servo output 8 and is assigned motor 40 "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:59
#: 47ec12391b624d758a850f0b0431af03
msgid ""
"In the case of dual heli frame with four servo swashplates, the RSCHeli "
"output function (Motor 31) will need to be assigned to another servo "
"output than its normal default of servo output 8."
msgstr ""

