#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:112
#: 18f59fab18134a73b024a93a37ded7ee
msgid "Check Proper Swashplate Movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:114
#: ad1eb245e42c4b0784c4aa0fb45fe1b1
msgid ""
"Use your transmitter to check for proper swashplate response to cyclic "
"and collective inputs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:116
#: b0696834c59b4d8aa729a5f4d20b65ca
msgid ""
"Push forward on the elevator stick and swashplate tilts forward; pull "
"back on the elevator stick and swashplate tilts aft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:117
#: 0be267d3f0c54d04859337be26ed4ac2
msgid ""
"Push right on the aileron stick and the swashplate tilts right; Push left"
" on the aileron stick and the swashplate tilts left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:118
#: 214ac8af22ec42bda8ce34c47a9d49e8
msgid ""
"Push up on the throttle stick (collective) and the swashplate will rise; "
"pull down on the throttle stick (collective) and the swashplate will "
"lower."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:120
#: f5578a6a288146ef954be113e8ae4402
msgid ""
"Set the :ref:`SERVO1_REVERSED <SERVO1_REVERSED>`, :ref:`SERVO2_REVERSED "
"<SERVO2_REVERSED>`, :ref:`SERVO3_REVERSED <SERVO3_REVERSED>`, and "
":ref:`H_SW_COL_DIR <H_SW_COL_DIR__AP_MotorsHeli_Single>` parameters so "
"that your swashplate responds correctly (as described above) to your "
"collective and cyclic inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:123
#: b7381b6c6ee7446a872421290733c162
msgid "Leveling your Swashplate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:125
#: 6e9401f5516e422485a9ed8b0f4f17fe
msgid ""
"The swashplate can be leveled using either a tool specially designed to "
"keep the swashplate perpendicular to the shaft or, a less expensive way, "
"using a magnet and nail (shown below). Using the magnet and nail won’t "
"require you to remove your rotor head to level your swashplate. Rotate "
"the shaft so the nail passes over the swashplate arm.  Adjusts swashplate"
" using one of methods below so the nail touches the top of each "
"swashplate arm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:136
#: 51271830c57f431fb218ef16f9d0fe03
msgid "Leveling swashplate without using Linearize Servo Feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:138
#: 9a98dc860206438d9360119279a9c768
msgid ""
"If you aren’t using the Linearize Servo feature, then you will use the "
"servo trim parameters to level your swashplate. Set the :ref:`H_SV_MAN "
"<H_SV_MAN>` parameter to 1.  Adjust the transmitter throttle stick "
"(collective) until the servos are nearly perpendicular to the shaft.  "
"Adjust :ref:`SERVO1_TRIM <SERVO1_TRIM>`, :ref:`SERVO2_TRIM "
"<SERVO2_TRIM>`, and :ref:`SERVO3_TRIM <SERVO3_TRIM>` until the swashplate"
" is level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:144
#: 370375d569364601b115e70ce88e77cd
msgid "Leveling swashplate using Linearize Servo Feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:146
#: ce3e5211b7d74c2eabbd10cc97edda48
msgid ""
"If you intend to use Linearize Servo feature then you will have to level "
"your swashplate using the pitch links that connects swashplate to the "
"servo. First though, you will set your servo so that at the midpoint of "
"the servo travel, the arm is perpendicular to the pitch link which in "
"most cases will be perpendicular to the shaft as well. If the spline on "
"the servo control horn is not allowing you to get the servo arm "
"perpendicular to the shaft, then you can use the servo trim parameters to"
" make them perpendicular to the shaft. You want the trim as close to 1500"
" as you can get. Now you can adjust your pitch links to make the "
"swashplate level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:158
#: e43f833473f843ab8cadbacd4c0fe0de
msgid "Collective Pitch Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:160
#: cffa340bc2d447c0bc2baeaeeaf8b8f4
msgid ""
"Use the servo manual setting (:ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>` ) to move the "
"swashplate between min and max positions. At each position use the blade "
"pitch gauge to set the desired blade pitch.  A typical collective blade "
"pitch range is -2° to +12°. Fully aerobatic setups would use -12° to "
"+12°. For initial tests and normal autonomous operation, the narrower "
"range is recommended. See :ref:`traditional-helicopter-aerobatic-setup` "
"for more information about aerobatic setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:164
#: 852ce53de9fe49658e848dd3fc38aaed
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>` to 2 to have swashplate move to maximum "
"position.  Adjust :ref:`H_COL_MAX <H_COL_MAX>` until blade pitch angle "
"measures the desired maximum collective blade pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:167
#: 3701d0c0a7fb41dba4ce76b6b06e8e7f
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>` to 4 to have swashplate move to minimum "
"position.  Adjust :ref:`H_COL_MIN <H_COL_MIN>` until blade pitch angle "
"measures the desired minimum collective blade pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:170
#: 6ac9ccaee72c46aeaf2d9995ed5f8012
msgid ""
"Overall collective measurements must be made using the :ref:`H_SV_MAN "
"<H_SV_MAN>` parameter since these would be impacted and inaccurate if the"
" autopilot stabilization was active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:173
#: 532caa73cef940c39afccec351b162e2
msgid "Minimum and Maximum Collective Blade Pitch Angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:175
#: ad4a6490942c4e05af0bc598c84dd6c2
msgid ""
"For :ref:`H_COL_ANG_MAX <H_COL_ANG_MAX>`, enter the maximum collective "
"blade pitch angle in degrees that corresponds to :ref:`H_COL_MAX "
"<H_COL_MAX>`.  For :ref:`H_COL_ANG_MIN <H_COL_ANG_MIN>`, enter the "
"minimum collective blade pitch angle in degrees that corresponds to "
":ref:`H_COL_MIN <H_COL_MIN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:178
#: 0a99e2bf261f46b18b7e62e619e7f693
msgid "Zero Thrust Point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:180
#: fb6ced8e74444579a37aee6a63cb4d17
msgid ""
":ref:`H_COL_ZERO_THRST <H_COL_ZERO_THRST>` is the collective blade pitch "
"angle in degrees for zero thrust.  The collective blade pitch that "
"corresponds to zero thrust is used to set the mixing of collective to "
"yaw.  This will be zero degrees collective blade pitch angle for "
"symmetric blades. Set the servo manual setting :ref:`H_SV_MAN <H_SV_MAN>`"
" to 3 to have swashplate move to zero thrust position and verify the "
"collective blade pitch corresponds the pitch angle set for "
":ref:`H_COL_ZERO_THRST <H_COL_ZERO_THRST>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:183
#: 53eeba84b63c48f083e61ec6e5853066
msgid "Minimum Landed Collective"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:185
#: 6c984a4d319149269ac6dc81b73452b5
msgid ""
"The :ref:`H_COL_LAND_MIN <H_COL_LAND_MIN>` parameter is used as the lower"
" collective pitch limit in degrees for modes that use altitude hold in "
"the vertical axis.  This keeps the autopilot from driving collective too "
"low resulting in ground resonance and is also used to detect landing in "
"these modes. The default angle for :ref:`H_COL_LAND_MIN <H_COL_LAND_MIN>`"
" parameter is set to -2 degrees collective blade pitch angle and would "
"allow symmetrical blade equipped vehicles to descend at a reasonable "
"rate, yet avoid being too negative on the ground.  If you have non-"
"symmetrical blades, then set it to a blade pitch that is lower by the "
"amount used as the zero thrust pitch angle.  For example, if the "
":ref:`H_COL_ZERO_THRST <H_COL_ZERO_THRST>` is determined to be -3 deg "
"then :ref:`H_COL_LAND_MIN <H_COL_LAND_MIN>` should be set to -5 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:187
#: c85cecc2294e400688fe7bf959ff7e51
msgid ""
"The default value for this parameter should be low enough to protect most"
" helicopters from in-flight disarm during autonomous flight due to false "
"landing detections.  This most likely will occur in conditions where the "
"aircraft experiences updrafts in hover or during landing phases of flight"
" which causes the collective to decrease below this parameter value.  "
"Acrobatic helicopter setups or heli's using non-symmetric blades should "
"consider lowering this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:190
#: d3a32fbe36c6488794f7d06e6ccebcd8
msgid "STABILIZED Collective Curve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-swashplate-setup.rst:192
